From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nuno5645 <ntrjferreira@hotmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 01:11:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] NSP script: merged NSPs and XCIs that hold the base game,
 updates and DLC

A merged NSP (or an XCI with the base game and an update on the cartridge) holds more than one title: the scan took the
package as the base game alone and the build failed or left the update out. nx_extract --contents lists every content meta
(type, title ID, version); the scan counts a merged package as base, update and DLC, the update is opened as a Patch,
each DLC is picked from the package by its title ID, and the extraction progress counts the shared file once.

Tested: Mario Kart 8 Deluxe from one merged NSP (base, update, DLC) builds for the Mac; test_nsp_scan.Merged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream-Status: backport 8ef752a2
Reason: merged NSPs and XCIs with an update are common dumps; upstream took it as 8ef752a2 (seedds/nxnative#842), so the next bump drops this patch
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#376

